msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "A call on the VHF radio. Help if you can; some calls bring a forecast."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "A fish on the line: press {reel_in} and reel with good timing."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "A long passage: the passage panel lets hours pass quickly, and the voyage map shows the way."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "A weather warning stops fast time. The chart's Weather tab shows what is coming along the course."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json src/ui/boat_care_menu.gd:137 src/ui/laptop/laptop_view.gd:321 src/ui/laptop/laptop_view.gd:652
msgid "Aboard"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Anchoring"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "At anchor. If the anchor drags the alarm sounds; the windlass raises it again."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Below deck: things that light up can be used with {interact}. The laptop on the table holds your achievements, postcards and travel updates."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Boats"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Click a harbour nearby and plan a course to it."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Companions"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json src/ui/hud.gd:183
msgid "Controls"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Cook at the galley stove in the cabin; a meal takes a little time. Make coffee, carry the mug, and set it in the cup holder on deck."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json src/ui/difficulty_menu.gd:13
msgid "Difficulty"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Each harbour has its own services, each in its own building on the quay: walk up the walkway from the guest pontoon. A grocery (food, water, a new hat, lures) with the fishmonger's stall beside it, a boatyard (boat care, haul-out and boats for sale) with the chandlery and the sail loft, a café, the harbour office and the noticeboard, and a lane into town (Go Ashore). The shops keep opening hours on the harbour's own clock; at a closed door you can wait until it opens, and the harbour office's hatch is always open for food and an emergency repair. The arrival card says what is there."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json src/boat/boat_area.gd:1170
msgid "Fishing"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Food and water"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Food and water are used every day, at sea and in harbour. The provisions locker in the cabin shows how many days are left; buy more at a grocery. The game warns you when stores run low."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Go back aboard and choose Set sail on the wheel."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Go on deck, open the chart, choose a harbour and plan a course, then set sail. Time runs while you sail: the buttons at the top of the screen pause it or make it run 5 or 20 times faster. The boat follows the course by itself; you can sleep, fish or cook on the way, and anything important will stop time and tell you."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Go on deck: walk to the companionway and press {interact}, or choose Go on deck on the wheel."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Harbour services"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "In harbour"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "In harbour the laptop at the cabin table offers remote work for pay by the hour. Voyages, new harbours, objectives, postcards and your little game earn renown; publish a travel update from the laptop to share it, which also earns a little money."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "In harbour: services differ from port to port. The arrival card said what is here; the work station pays for remote work while moored."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Let time run"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Life aboard"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Long passages"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Make it home on the cabin's wheel lets you place cabin things you have bought; the framed world map lets you dream of voyages and plan one from it."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Making the cabin home"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Mind the hat: strong wind on deck can blow it away. {captains_hat} takes it off."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Money, work and renown"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Night falls. The berth in the cabin is a fine place to sleep; anything important will wake you."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "On long passages the passage panel lets hours pass quickly while the voyage map shows the boat crossing the sea. Everything that would stop time still does."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "On the laptop, choose Your little game. Pick a task (2 to 4 hours), answer its small question and work; milestones fill the devlog and earn renown, and the release brings the first sales. An interrupted session keeps the hours worked."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "On the laptop, open Publications and make a postcard. Pick what it shows (harbours, catches, your companion, voyages, weather and evening light), the words and the layout, then make and publish it: it takes about two hours. Each subject earns renown once; every card goes in the scrapbook."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Open the chart"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Open the chart at the navigation table or from the wheel. Click a harbour (or search for one) and plan a course; drag the course line to add a waypoint, and select a waypoint and press {delete_waypoint} to remove it. The tabs show the course, the weather along it and the details. Zoom with {map_zoom_in} and {map_zoom_out}."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Open the chart: Charts on the wheel, or the navigation table in the cabin."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Open the menu with {pause} to save in one of three slots or load. Aboard, {quicksave} quicksaves and {quickload} loads the quicksave."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Other ships sail too. If one is on a collision course a warning sounds and the radar opens by itself while the risk lasts. A call on the VHF radio can ask for help or bring a forecast."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Plan a course"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json src/ui/postcard_menu.gd:28
msgid "Postcards from the Sea"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Press {action_wheel} to open the action wheel. It shows what you can do here. Close it with {pause}."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Press {captains_log} to open the Captain's Log, then close it again."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Relaxed, Standard or Seasoned Captain changes starting money, how fast stores are used, wear, weather damage, costs and the rescue fee; the weather itself is the same. Change it any time from the menu: it counts from then on."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Renown earned! Publish a travel update in harbour to share it (the work station or the Captain's Log)."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json src/navigation/vessel_profile.gd:21
msgid "Sailing"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Saving and loading"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json src/app/app.gd:802 src/app/app.gd:930 src/navigation/world_map.tscn:343
msgid "Set sail"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Set sail from the wheel once a course is planned. The boat sails the course by itself. The instruments show the speed, the heading, the wind and the route, on deck and in the cabin; {instruments} (or a click on them) shows them close up with their pages, and {chartplotter} the chartplotter at the helm. The wheel offers the radar, and a chandlery sells better instruments. {sail_trim} (or the winch on the cockpit coaming) opens sail trim: well-trimmed sails are faster."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Set the rod on deck from its holder or the wheel and choose a lure. When a fish bites a bell rings: press {reel_in} and reel it in with good timing. Keep fish in the cool box, release them, sell them at the fishmonger or cook them."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Settings and tips"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Settings has the volumes (also the wind on its own), display, interface size and light, language and accessibility. Tips can be turned off there. This Handbook is always here: {handbook} or Captain's Handbook in the menu."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Sleep in the berth for 1 to 12 hours. The world goes on while you sleep, and anything important wakes you."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Sleeping"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Stores are running low: a grocery in harbour sells food and water."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "The Captain's Log"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "The Captain's hat"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "The action wheel"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "The boat sails the course by itself. Try 5× or 20× at the top of the screen; anything important stops time again."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "The boat's condition and rescue"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "The cabin"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "The cabin has your berth (sleep), the navigation table (the chart) with the logbook and the VHF radio on it, the switch panel (what the boat keeps track of), the sea chest by the berth (make the cabin home), the provisions locker, your laptop on the table, the galley stove, the coffee table, the hat hook, the framed world map and the trophy board; your newest postcard lies on the table. Things you can use light up when you are close; press {interact}, and {pause} puts them back."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "The chart and planning a course"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "The chart: click a harbour to plan a course; drag the line to add a waypoint. The tabs show the weather and the details."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "The galley and coffee"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "The hull, rig and engine wear with miles, time and weather. A boatyard can service and repair them and haul the boat out. If the boat is badly damaged at sea you are rescued and brought to harbour, for a fee."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "The laptop and your achievements"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "The world has one clock. The buttons at the top pause time or run it at 1, 5 or 20 times. On long passages a passage panel can run hours per second. Sleeping, working and the pastimes pass hours at once: the screen fades, the clock counts, and you come back at normal speed. Warnings, a fish on the line, the anchor alarm, traffic, a radio call and arriving all stop time early."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "This harbour has a boatyard on its quay, with a chandlery and a sail loft beside it: boat care and boats for sale. Walk up the pontoon's walkway to the quay."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Time and speed"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Traffic, radar and radio"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Traffic: a ship on a collision course. The radar shows it until the risk has passed."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Underway"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Underway! {sail_trim} trims the sails, {instruments} shows the instruments close up, {chartplotter} the chartplotter, and the time buttons at the top make the passage go faster."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Underway, the windlass on the foredeck (or Anchor on the wheel) drops the anchor where the bottom allows. The anchor alarm sounds if it drags. On the chart at the navigation table you can select a waypoint and press {anchorage_key} to make it an anchorage: the boat stops there and asks whether to anchor or sail on."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Up on deck"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Walk about"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Walk around the boat with {move}."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Walk with {move}. Press {interact} next to something that lights up to use it. {action_wheel} opens the action wheel with what you can do where you stand. {captains_log} opens the Captain's Log, {captains_hat} puts your hat on or takes it off, and {pause} opens the menu (and closes any window). {handbook} opens this Handbook."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json src/navigation/world_map.gd:146 src/navigation/world_map.gd:957
msgid "Weather"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Weather and safety"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Well done, Captain: you are on your way. Everything else is in the Captain's Handbook ({handbook})."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Wind and weather change with time and place; the chart's Weather tab shows what is coming along your course. A weather warning stops fast time and sleep. Strong wind and storms wear the boat and can damage it."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "You set out alone - but perhaps not for long. Now and then, arriving in a harbour, you may find a small cardboard box on the pontoon with a Ragdoll, a Pug or a little conure in it. Say hello with {interact}, offer a treat, play a little; if it decides to follow you, the companionway asks whether to welcome it aboard (with a name, if you like) or let it go home with the girl who knows it. Up to two companions can live aboard. They follow you between cabin and deck and nap where they like; the conure flies between its favourite perches. Walk up and press {interact} to pet one. In harbour they come ashore with you; the boat cannot cast off while one is still ashore, so call them aboard (the wheel, or when you set sail). They are by the berth when you wake, and on long passages you will find yourself talking to them now and then."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "You start with your first boat. At a boatyard you can buy another boat for its price; boats you own stay yours, and you can move aboard any of them at a boatyard."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json src/app/app.gd:561
msgid "Your first voyage"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Your game"
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "Your laptop sits on the cabin table: use it with {interact} (or Laptop on the wheel). Home shows your renown and what you did lately; Publications holds postcards and travel updates; Achievements is your collection, in categories, the unlocked ones first and newest at the top, each with when, where and on which boat you earned it (older ones say \"Previously unlocked\"); Voyage history shows your records, among them your best hour and best day under sail. Speed achievements count only a whole hour (or day) under sail, never the engine. Esc closes the laptop."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "{action_wheel} opens a wheel with what makes sense where you are: in the cabin sleep, the world map, the chart table, provisions and the laptop; on deck the charts, the fishing rod and, underway, the chart plotter, the instruments, radar, sail trim and anchor. On/off items show a check mark."
msgstr ""

#: data/academy/academy.json
msgid "{captains_hat} puts the hat on or takes it off. On deck in strong wind it can blow away: the game warns you first, and below deck or ashore it is safe. A lost hat can be replaced at a grocery in harbour."
msgstr ""

